# NexusPour ERP - Engineering & Architectural Rules
# Intellectual Property & Architecture: Omid Pourmahmoud

## 1. MANDATORY ZERO GHOST UI RULE
- Whenever a role's permission or business logic changes, YOU MUST UPDATE ALL CORRESPONDING JINJA2 HTML TEMPLATES, FORMS, TABLES, MODALS, AND PRINT SLIPS.
- NEVER leave a button, menu link, form `<input>`, or table `<th>/<td>` visible to a user who lacks permission to use or view it.
- Relying solely on backend `403 Forbidden` is considered a CRITICAL BUG. Wrap restricted elements in strict Jinja2 role conditionals (`{% if ... %}`).

## 2. STRICT TOP-DOWN HIERARCHY & BLIND RECEIVING/WEIGHING
- Warehouse Supervisor (`warehouse`) operates blind to financial figures (unit price, total cost, landed cost, financial kardex).
- Weighbridge Operator (`baskool`) operates blind to counterparty identities (supplier/customer names) and financial prices. Weighing is bound to reference orders (`PO-xxxx` / `SO-xxxx`).

## 3. SEMANTIC VERSIONING & AUTO-BUMP RULE
- Whenever a new feature, architectural change, or bug-fix cycle is completed, automatically increment the patch/minor version in `src/core/version.py` and append a professional enterprise release note entry to `RELEASE_HISTORY` with the current timestamp.

## 4. ONE-WORD `/hunt` AUDIT TRIGGER
- Typing `/hunt` or `hunt` triggers the complete 4-layer audit (`tests/deep_bug_hunter.py`).
- All tests must pass 100% with zero bugs, zero 500/422 errors, zero ghost UI leaks, and full E2E workflow integrity.
